    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "im not so sure about the \"unstoppable force\" thing. if the tech only advances because companies choose to pour billions into R&D to cut labor costs, isn't that just a deliberate economic strategy rather than some kind of natural evolution? feels like saying \"the weather is changing\" when we're actually talking about how we build cities.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
